 "slot_change_request": "QW-SRAM3 10-19: same RTL/params/pins as closed qfd_tt_ctlm_head; only the two 64x512 program SRAMs bind the <=5.21 pins/um successor ot_sram_1r1w_64x512_m1_r2c2_p192_mir (171.288x153.912, W/E 793 pins at 0.192 um; old master 10.2 pins/um). p192d FAIL only on TT pin-flop spread 84.6 (FF 72.3; GRT ovf 0): clock entered at the SW corner (S face 6-7.5 um), 713 um Manhattan to the far pin flops -> clk moved to the W-face centre (225-228 um, provisional die pin). Bit-sliced p192_bs master (no W<->E data crossing).",
 "pin_regs": {
  "enable": false,
  "reason": "Unchanged closed qfd_tt_ctlm_head RTL registers every port at the face (io_flop_at_pins cols 4 places those flops FIRM at their pins, inhold/outhold); adding generated pin regs would add a cycle to every head port, outside this SRAM-only change"
 },
